1
00:01:31,660 --> 00:01:35,060
[In my prime]

2
00:01:35,310 --> 00:01:37,789
[Episode 16]

3
00:01:40,200 --> 00:01:40,660
Auntie,

4
00:01:42,479 --> 00:01:45,210
could you lend me some money
to pay for my tuition?

5
00:01:46,080 --> 00:01:47,350
When I get a job and make money

6
00:01:47,350 --> 00:01:48,450
in the future,

7
00:01:48,950 --> 00:01:49,539
I will

8
00:01:49,920 --> 00:01:52,120
absolutely pay you back with interest.

9
00:02:08,240 --> 00:02:08,639
Hello?

10
00:02:10,710 --> 00:02:12,590
Hello. Auntie, it...

11
00:02:12,820 --> 00:02:14,630
it is me, Qi Shi.

12
00:02:16,030 --> 00:02:17,160
Oh, it's you, Qi Shi.

13
00:02:18,310 --> 00:02:19,120
How did you do

14
00:02:19,120 --> 00:02:20,780
on the college entrance exam?

15
00:02:24,030 --> 00:02:26,150
I... performed poorly.

16
00:02:28,400 --> 00:02:29,470
That's no big deal.

17
00:02:29,840 --> 00:02:31,190
I only finished middle school,

18
00:02:31,190 --> 00:02:33,050
yet I managed to become a big boss.

19
00:02:33,120 --> 00:02:35,310
Many staffers of my company
are college grads.

20
00:02:35,310 --> 00:02:36,800
They know much about theories, but lack

21
00:02:36,800 --> 00:02:37,860
practical skills.

22
00:02:38,470 --> 00:02:39,380
In my opinion, you are

23
00:02:39,380 --> 00:02:40,120
better off entering

24
00:02:40,120 --> 00:02:41,280
the real world early.

25
00:02:41,280 --> 00:02:43,090
Diplomas are nothing
but just pieces of paper.

26
00:02:43,090 --> 00:02:44,000
However high your degree is,

27
00:02:44,000 --> 00:02:46,520
you'll still have to apply
what you've learned, right?

28
00:02:46,520 --> 00:02:47,920
You can succeed anywhere

29
00:02:48,190 --> 00:02:50,190
as long as you have the right skills.

30
00:02:52,800 --> 00:02:53,960
You gave me a call.

31
00:02:54,030 --> 00:02:55,290
Has something come up?

32
00:03:07,000 --> 00:03:08,680
I don't want to go to a special school!

33
00:03:08,680 --> 00:03:10,030
I'll stay in the yard all night

34
00:03:10,030 --> 00:03:12,490
if Mom still doesn't allow me
to go to school!

35
00:03:15,190 --> 00:03:16,840
Does drinking soy sauce
really make you darker?

36
00:03:16,840 --> 00:03:17,770
She really knows

37
00:03:18,190 --> 00:03:19,720
how to solve this equation.

38
00:03:19,840 --> 00:03:21,240
This is incredibly rare!

39
00:03:30,570 --> 00:03:32,360
Since I was little,
they called me "White-Haired Girl"

40
00:03:32,360 --> 00:03:33,680
and called me a monster.

41
00:03:33,680 --> 00:03:35,079
I refused to just take it,

42
00:03:35,150 --> 00:03:36,240
so I fought them.

43
00:03:37,360 --> 00:03:38,960
I ran for class monitor

44
00:03:40,360 --> 00:03:42,160
and asked to join the sports meet

45
00:03:43,430 --> 00:03:45,030
just in order to prove myself

46
00:03:45,360 --> 00:03:47,280
to be the same as everyone of you.

47
00:03:50,120 --> 00:03:51,800
I just wanted a chance,

48
00:03:54,430 --> 00:03:56,680
a fair chance to compete.

49
00:03:57,910 --> 00:03:58,640
I might lose.

50
00:03:59,590 --> 00:04:00,310
But even so, I wanted

51
00:04:00,310 --> 00:04:02,110
a chance to lose fair and square.

52
00:05:01,920 --> 00:05:02,750
Today, let me

53
00:05:02,950 --> 00:05:04,350
tell you some more words.

54
00:05:05,120 --> 00:05:06,510
The wise are free from doubt.

55
00:05:06,510 --> 00:05:07,870
The benevolent are free from worry.

56
00:05:07,870 --> 00:05:09,390
The brave are free from fear.

57
00:05:09,390 --> 00:05:11,290
Diplomas are nothing
but just pieces of paper.

58
00:05:11,290 --> 00:05:12,120
However high your degree is,

59
00:05:12,120 --> 00:05:14,510
you'll still have to apply
what you've learned, right?

60
00:05:14,510 --> 00:05:15,870
You can succeed anywhere

61
00:05:15,870 --> 00:05:17,870
as long as you have the right skills.

62
00:06:02,830 --> 00:06:03,270
Qi Shi,

63
00:06:04,240 --> 00:06:05,370
where are you off to?

64
00:06:05,830 --> 00:06:07,040
I'm not repeating the year.

65
00:06:07,040 --> 00:06:07,870
These are useless now.

66
00:06:07,870 --> 00:06:09,000
So I'll go sell them.

67
00:06:09,680 --> 00:06:10,540
Give them to me.

68
00:06:10,600 --> 00:06:11,460
Give them to me.

69
00:06:12,700 --> 00:06:13,480
Aren't you too young

70
00:06:13,480 --> 00:06:15,080
to give up on your education?

71
00:06:16,190 --> 00:06:16,790
Come here.

72
00:06:18,870 --> 00:06:19,620
Take this money.

73
00:06:19,620 --> 00:06:20,270
-Retake the college entrance exam.
-No.

74
00:06:20,270 --> 00:06:21,530
-No, I can't.
-Take it.

75
00:06:22,040 --> 00:06:22,920
If you need anything,

76
00:06:22,920 --> 00:06:24,000
just let me know.

77
00:06:24,310 --> 00:06:26,120
I will support you unconditionally.

78
00:06:26,120 --> 00:06:26,600
Just take it.

79
00:06:26,600 --> 00:06:27,660
Thank you, Mr. Cao.

80
00:06:27,830 --> 00:06:29,690
But I really don't need the money.

81
00:06:29,830 --> 00:06:30,270
Qi Shi,

82
00:06:30,960 --> 00:06:32,190
whatever between me and your parents

83
00:06:32,190 --> 00:06:33,920
has nothing to do with you kids.

84
00:06:34,000 --> 00:06:34,700
Just consider

85
00:06:34,700 --> 00:06:36,159
the money as a loan from me.

86
00:06:36,360 --> 00:06:37,310
You can pay me back

87
00:06:37,310 --> 00:06:38,920
when you are able to someday, alright?

88
00:06:38,920 --> 00:06:39,680
Mr. Cao,

89
00:06:40,310 --> 00:06:41,370
you're truly nice.

90
00:06:41,650 --> 00:06:42,800
I'm not refusing your money

91
00:06:42,800 --> 00:06:43,820
because of the grudges

92
00:06:43,820 --> 00:06:45,070
between you and my parents.

93
00:06:45,070 --> 00:06:46,730
I've just thought it through.

94
00:06:47,800 --> 00:06:48,930
There are many paths

95
00:06:49,390 --> 00:06:51,000
to choose from in life.

96
00:06:51,870 --> 00:06:53,950
Going to college isn't the only option.

97
00:06:53,950 --> 00:06:55,390
You see, many successful people

98
00:06:55,390 --> 00:06:56,480
dropped out of school.

99
00:06:56,480 --> 00:06:58,500
Didn't they go on top
of the world in the end?

100
00:06:58,500 --> 00:06:59,110
Besides,

101
00:06:59,159 --> 00:07:01,750
there are night schools
and adult self-study exams.

102
00:07:01,750 --> 00:07:03,150
As long as I want to learn,

103
00:07:03,240 --> 00:07:04,370
I can do it anywhere.

104
00:07:04,480 --> 00:07:05,360
But instead of going

105
00:07:05,360 --> 00:07:06,680
to college, what can you do?

106
00:07:06,680 --> 00:07:08,540
I'll step out into the real world.

107
00:07:09,160 --> 00:07:10,090
I'm leaving home

108
00:07:10,560 --> 00:07:11,560
to make my own way.

109
00:07:11,560 --> 00:07:13,240
Where can you possibly go
when you leave home?

110
00:07:13,240 --> 00:07:14,640
You're just a young girl.

111
00:07:17,000 --> 00:07:18,260
I haven't decided yet.

112
00:07:25,070 --> 00:07:26,950
I just want to prove to my mom

113
00:07:27,600 --> 00:07:28,660
that she was wrong.

114
00:07:29,120 --> 00:07:29,950
My life won't

115
00:07:30,560 --> 00:07:32,090
turn out like what she said.

116
00:07:33,190 --> 00:07:34,190
I have the right

117
00:07:34,600 --> 00:07:36,070
to choose my own path.

118
00:07:37,070 --> 00:07:38,200
And I firmly believe

119
00:07:38,750 --> 00:07:40,280
that I can make it to the end.

120
00:07:45,720 --> 00:07:46,980
If you ever need money,

121
00:07:47,080 --> 00:07:48,350
just let me know.

122
00:08:28,680 --> 00:08:30,360
Congratulations, Qi Zhi.

123
00:08:30,750 --> 00:08:32,880
You've brought honor to your country.

124
00:08:35,720 --> 00:08:37,580
Thank you, President. Thank you!

125
00:09:11,690 --> 00:09:15,100
[Shuttles
between Qingwu Town and Jiangyuan City]

126
00:09:18,200 --> 00:09:18,730
Sweetie.

127
00:09:20,450 --> 00:09:22,450
Have you really thought it through?

128
00:09:39,360 --> 00:09:40,630
Take this money.

129
00:09:41,200 --> 00:09:42,150
Remember to treat

130
00:09:42,150 --> 00:09:43,550
yourself well out there.

131
00:09:46,150 --> 00:09:47,480
I'm not capable of much.

132
00:09:47,870 --> 00:09:49,750
This is all I can do to help you.

133
00:09:55,550 --> 00:09:57,280
Where did this money come from?

134
00:09:58,150 --> 00:09:59,120
You kept a secret stash

135
00:09:59,120 --> 00:10:00,790
behind my mom's back again,huh?

136
00:10:00,790 --> 00:10:01,870
What secret stash?

137
00:10:03,000 --> 00:10:03,960
I saved this up bit by bit

138
00:10:03,960 --> 00:10:06,320
by secretly collecting and selling scrap.

139
00:10:06,320 --> 00:10:07,920
I meant it as my pocket money.

140
00:10:10,120 --> 00:10:10,750
Oh, right.

141
00:10:11,480 --> 00:10:12,030
And this.

142
00:10:15,600 --> 00:10:16,600
It's secondhand.

143
00:10:17,720 --> 00:10:19,450
I've tested all the functions.

144
00:10:20,000 --> 00:10:20,800
It works fine.

145
00:10:21,080 --> 00:10:22,790
If you can, call home often.

146
00:10:24,080 --> 00:10:26,030
I put some credit on it, so don't worry

147
00:10:26,030 --> 00:10:27,230
about the phone bill.

148
00:10:36,390 --> 00:10:37,520
I'll take them both.

149
00:10:37,790 --> 00:10:39,450
It's time I got on the bus, Dad.

150
00:10:40,330 --> 00:10:41,320
Hold on, hold on.

151
00:10:51,670 --> 00:10:52,530
You look great.

152
00:10:54,650 --> 00:10:55,080
Take care

153
00:10:55,080 --> 00:10:56,520
of your health out there.

154
00:10:58,230 --> 00:10:58,960
I'm leaving.

155
00:10:59,000 --> 00:10:59,530
Go ahead.

156
00:11:13,720 --> 00:11:14,250
Sweetie,

157
00:11:14,840 --> 00:11:17,080
if things don't go well
in the provincial capital,

158
00:11:17,080 --> 00:11:17,940
just come back.

159
00:11:18,480 --> 00:11:20,740
We'll always have a place
for you at home.

160
00:11:21,670 --> 00:11:22,670
Don't worry, Dad.

161
00:11:22,960 --> 00:11:24,360
That day will never come.

162
00:11:26,030 --> 00:11:28,030
Just wait till I make it big.

163
00:11:28,600 --> 00:11:30,860
Then I'll create a life of luxury for you.

164
00:11:33,870 --> 00:11:34,440
Go home.

165
00:11:35,390 --> 00:11:36,050
Go home now!

166
00:12:20,720 --> 00:12:22,480
Our family used to be so happy.

167
00:12:24,270 --> 00:12:25,030
Even though

168
00:12:25,480 --> 00:12:26,840
life was a bit hard,

169
00:12:27,790 --> 00:12:30,190
at least both our kids were at home,
so we had

170
00:12:31,600 --> 00:12:33,000
something to strive for.

171
00:12:34,550 --> 00:12:36,480
Now our son is away,

172
00:12:37,600 --> 00:12:39,330
and our daughter has also left.

173
00:12:44,750 --> 00:12:46,410
What's the point of our lives?

174
00:12:49,270 --> 00:12:50,670
Though our kids are away,

175
00:12:50,670 --> 00:12:52,530
I'm still here with you, aren't I?

176
00:13:00,960 --> 00:13:02,360
How does that saying go?

177
00:13:03,870 --> 00:13:05,600
When things hit rock bottom...

178
00:13:14,510 --> 00:13:16,120
Good days come

179
00:13:18,360 --> 00:13:19,820
once the bad days are over.

180
00:13:25,720 --> 00:13:28,050
You should always look on the bright side.

181
00:13:30,750 --> 00:13:32,080
Things will get better.

182
00:13:37,240 --> 00:13:37,960
They will.

183
00:13:53,760 --> 00:13:57,720
♪ The wind blew through our hair ♪

184
00:14:00,410 --> 00:14:04,090
♪ The story slowly grew complicated ♪

185
00:14:07,070 --> 00:14:12,080
♪ We didn't become anyone's legend ♪

186
00:14:13,000 --> 00:14:18,080
♪ We only learned to grow up in the rain ♪

187
00:14:20,740 --> 00:14:24,330
♪ Are we to blame fate? ♪

188
00:14:26,830 --> 00:14:30,880
♪ Adulthood is bandaging your own fall ♪

189
00:14:33,500 --> 00:14:36,540
♪ Rented rooms, the last bus home ♪

190
00:14:35,720 --> 00:14:36,960
Take this once a day.

191
00:14:36,560 --> 00:14:38,790
♪ What does the future hold? ♪

192
00:14:39,410 --> 00:14:44,080
♪ It's been long since I last had
the guts to say I feared ♪

193
00:14:47,560 --> 00:14:50,950
♪ Though we have nothing,
we still bustle about ♪

194
00:14:53,650 --> 00:14:57,950
♪ Because the answer is clear
as long as you are around ♪

195
00:15:00,030 --> 00:15:02,140
♪ The old dreams are now covered in dust ♪

196
00:15:02,160 --> 00:15:04,620
♪ But it's okay ♪

197
00:15:07,050 --> 00:15:13,100
♪ Some things are better off
staying the way they are ♪

198
00:15:14,360 --> 00:15:18,600
[Welcome to Haizhou]

199
00:15:32,840 --> 00:15:34,100
Look, I do the same work

200
00:15:34,510 --> 00:15:36,440
in Haizhou as I did in Qingwu,

201
00:15:36,790 --> 00:15:37,530
but I can make

202
00:15:37,630 --> 00:15:39,360
500 yuan more every month here.

203
00:15:39,550 --> 00:15:40,950
Haizhou is a great place.

204
00:15:41,440 --> 00:15:42,870
I'm just not sure what job

205
00:15:42,170 --> 00:15:46,420
♪ Who hasn't panicked
in this fast-paced world? ♪

206
00:15:43,320 --> 00:15:44,650
my education can get me.

207
00:15:45,360 --> 00:15:46,160
In big cities,

208
00:15:46,670 --> 00:15:48,530
skills matter more than degrees.

209
00:15:48,850 --> 00:15:54,920
♪ All I see is the look in your eyes ♪

210
00:15:48,960 --> 00:15:50,550
My niece only finished middle school,

211
00:15:50,550 --> 00:15:52,010
but she runs a company now.

212
00:15:52,360 --> 00:15:54,120
She even bought a villa for her family.

213
00:15:54,120 --> 00:15:54,720
Really?

214
00:15:55,030 --> 00:15:55,580
Of course.

215
00:15:55,580 --> 00:16:00,170
♪ If there's nothing left tomorrow ♪

216
00:15:56,980 --> 00:15:58,980
Haizhou really is an amazing place.

217
00:16:02,390 --> 00:16:13,080
♪ I'll still walk home with you ♪

218
00:18:01,340 --> 00:18:02,200
I can't hold up.

219
00:18:45,600 --> 00:18:46,210
Sorry.

220
00:18:46,240 --> 00:18:46,510
We really

221
00:18:46,510 --> 00:18:48,110
don't have any hiring plans.

222
00:18:48,550 --> 00:18:49,830
I've been to every office
in this building.

223
00:18:49,830 --> 00:18:51,000
I... must find a job now,

224
00:18:51,000 --> 00:18:52,590
or I'll end up sleeping on the streets.

225
00:18:52,590 --> 00:18:53,050
Well...

226
00:18:53,790 --> 00:18:54,240
How about this?

227
00:18:54,240 --> 00:18:55,110
I'm begging you.

228
00:18:55,110 --> 00:18:56,310
Please just let me see

229
00:18:57,080 --> 00:18:57,790
the company's...

230
00:18:57,790 --> 00:18:58,550
Seek opportunities

231
00:18:58,550 --> 00:18:59,210
elsewhere.

232
00:18:59,270 --> 00:18:59,790
Did you just say

233
00:18:59,790 --> 00:19:01,270
you couldn't do a tiny task like this?

234
00:19:01,270 --> 00:19:01,730
What?

235
00:19:01,830 --> 00:19:03,270
You want me to turn on the computer

236
00:19:03,270 --> 00:19:04,550
and make the slides for you?

237
00:19:04,550 --> 00:19:04,960
Zhou!

238
00:19:05,440 --> 00:19:05,830
Zhou!

239
00:19:06,070 --> 00:19:06,670
Come over!

240
00:19:06,960 --> 00:19:07,560
Mail this.

241
00:19:07,750 --> 00:19:08,440
Got it, Mr. He.

242
00:19:08,440 --> 00:19:10,200
Take my post as the manager then!

243
00:19:10,200 --> 00:19:11,240
Get lost if you can't do your job!

244
00:19:11,240 --> 00:19:12,100
I'm competent!

245
00:19:12,200 --> 00:19:12,930
Very much so.

246
00:19:13,240 --> 00:19:13,900
Who are you?

247
00:19:15,270 --> 00:19:16,070
Hello, Mr. He.

248
00:19:16,440 --> 00:19:17,370
My name is Qi Shi.

249
00:19:17,790 --> 00:19:18,440
I hope

250
00:19:18,750 --> 00:19:20,010
you can give me a chance

251
00:19:20,240 --> 00:19:21,550
to solve your problems

252
00:19:21,750 --> 00:19:22,750
and assist you...

253
00:19:24,190 --> 00:19:25,390
in many, many things!

254
00:19:25,440 --> 00:19:27,310
This is a legitimate company
we're running,

255
00:19:27,310 --> 00:19:28,640
not some street stall.

256
00:19:28,770 --> 00:19:29,640
We won't hire you simply

257
00:19:29,640 --> 00:19:30,920
because you stick around

258
00:19:30,920 --> 00:19:32,250
and say a few nice words.

259
00:19:33,000 --> 00:19:33,480
I know.

260
00:19:34,270 --> 00:19:35,920
This is a big company after all.

261
00:19:35,920 --> 00:19:38,180
I heard you're short-staffed right now.

262
00:19:38,350 --> 00:19:39,110
How about this?

263
00:19:39,110 --> 00:19:40,160
I'll work here, but you don't

264
00:19:40,160 --> 00:19:40,960
have to pay me.

265
00:19:41,270 --> 00:19:42,700
Could you consider giving

266
00:19:42,700 --> 00:19:43,200
me a chance

267
00:19:43,200 --> 00:19:44,660
to interview if you find me

268
00:19:44,790 --> 00:19:45,450
qualified?

269
00:19:48,720 --> 00:19:49,780
If I assign a helper

270
00:19:49,880 --> 00:19:50,720
to you for those slides,

271
00:19:50,720 --> 00:19:52,380
can you finish them in one day?

272
00:19:52,480 --> 00:19:52,790
Yes.

273
00:19:53,070 --> 00:19:55,530
So you can finish your work
with a helper now?

274
00:19:58,160 --> 00:19:58,510
Okay.

275
00:19:59,030 --> 00:19:59,760
Stay with her

276
00:20:00,200 --> 00:20:01,000
and work hard.

277
00:20:01,350 --> 00:20:02,950
Come see me when you're done.

278
00:20:06,640 --> 00:20:07,640
Thank you, Mr. He!

279
00:20:07,960 --> 00:20:08,490
Let's go.

280
00:20:17,400 --> 00:20:18,050
Your company

281
00:20:18,050 --> 00:20:19,660
is quite large.

282
00:20:21,000 --> 00:20:22,660
Do you know how to make slides?

283
00:20:23,510 --> 00:20:23,880
What?

284
00:20:26,070 --> 00:20:27,400
It's a computer software, right?

285
00:20:27,400 --> 00:20:28,270
I can learn.

286
00:20:28,760 --> 00:20:29,550
I could make them myself

287
00:20:29,550 --> 00:20:31,350
in the time it takes to teach you.

288
00:20:31,350 --> 00:20:33,210
Then what else can I help you with?

289
00:20:33,510 --> 00:20:34,310
You can leave now.

290
00:20:34,310 --> 00:20:35,960
This is my job anyway.

291
00:20:36,310 --> 00:20:37,550
I'll just hang in there

292
00:20:37,550 --> 00:20:38,410
and get it done.

293
00:20:38,590 --> 00:20:39,410
No way.

294
00:20:39,860 --> 00:20:40,960
I already said I'd help you.

295
00:20:40,960 --> 00:20:41,570
I must

296
00:20:41,790 --> 00:20:43,070
keep my word.

297
00:20:43,310 --> 00:20:44,350
I don't know how to make slides,

298
00:20:44,350 --> 00:20:45,810
but I can help you organize

299
00:20:45,930 --> 00:20:47,110
documents and stuff.

300
00:20:47,110 --> 00:20:47,950
I can do all that.

301
00:20:47,950 --> 00:20:49,550
Or I can buy food for you and get you

302
00:20:49,550 --> 00:20:50,030
water.

303
00:20:50,680 --> 00:20:51,000
I...

304
00:20:51,400 --> 00:20:52,270
I'll do anything

305
00:20:52,270 --> 00:20:53,070
you tell me to,

306
00:20:53,960 --> 00:20:55,790
except for using the toilet for you.

307
00:20:55,790 --> 00:20:56,990
Actually, you are...

308
00:20:57,920 --> 00:20:59,050
quite interesting.

309
00:21:01,440 --> 00:21:02,240
How about this?

310
00:21:02,240 --> 00:21:03,850
Extract all the underlined

311
00:21:03,880 --> 00:21:05,350
key information

312
00:21:05,720 --> 00:21:06,030
from

313
00:21:07,750 --> 00:21:08,680
this material,

314
00:21:09,110 --> 00:21:10,570
type it into the computer,

315
00:21:10,650 --> 00:21:11,680
and organize it into

316
00:21:11,680 --> 00:21:13,010
a structured document.

317
00:21:13,110 --> 00:21:14,400
Then I'll teach you

318
00:21:14,680 --> 00:21:15,720
how to make slides

319
00:21:15,720 --> 00:21:16,880
based on that document

320
00:21:16,880 --> 00:21:19,280
and form a report
for the leaders to review.

321
00:21:21,880 --> 00:21:22,880
Consider it done.

322
00:21:26,950 --> 00:21:28,510
Cao Xin, hurry up!

323
00:21:28,790 --> 00:21:30,400
Class is beginning.
It's a required course.

324
00:21:30,400 --> 00:21:32,400
That old man Wang will call the roll.

325
00:21:34,270 --> 00:21:36,120
Fine. See you in the back row.

326
00:21:41,330 --> 00:21:44,030
[Finance]

327
00:22:03,750 --> 00:22:04,950
He still won't see us?

328
00:22:08,590 --> 00:22:09,390
Okay, I got it.

329
00:22:18,380 --> 00:22:20,000
He must be blaming me.

330
00:22:27,960 --> 00:22:29,490
Blaming me for stopping him

331
00:22:30,070 --> 00:22:32,110
from dating Cao Si,

332
00:22:35,200 --> 00:22:36,800
for being useless and unable

333
00:22:38,240 --> 00:22:39,900
to get him a lighter sentence,

334
00:22:41,890 --> 00:22:43,200
and for neglecting his sister,

335
00:22:43,200 --> 00:22:45,440
leaving her to struggle alone

336
00:22:46,200 --> 00:22:47,510
in Haizhou.

337
00:22:48,310 --> 00:22:49,310
It's all my fault!

338
00:22:49,350 --> 00:22:50,120
My fault!

339
00:22:50,880 --> 00:22:51,680
Huo Qinglian,

340
00:22:51,680 --> 00:22:52,500
what are you doing?

341
00:22:52,500 --> 00:22:53,640
You are famous around here

342
00:22:53,640 --> 00:22:54,570
for being tough.

343
00:22:55,590 --> 00:22:57,060
Are you hitting

344
00:22:57,790 --> 00:22:59,050
and scolding yourself

345
00:22:59,350 --> 00:23:00,310
now that you can't

346
00:23:00,310 --> 00:23:01,640
v-vent it out on others?

347
00:23:01,960 --> 00:23:02,960
What's wrong with that?

348
00:23:02,960 --> 00:23:03,820
Can't I do that?

349
00:23:05,240 --> 00:23:05,700
You can.

350
00:23:06,790 --> 00:23:07,650
You surely can.

351
00:23:07,790 --> 00:23:08,990
As long as you want to.

352
00:23:11,000 --> 00:23:12,240
You're Huo Qinglian.

353
00:23:12,270 --> 00:23:13,730
What have you ever feared?

354
00:23:15,830 --> 00:23:16,360
Nothing.

355
00:23:18,550 --> 00:23:19,680
Everything's fine.

356
00:23:48,270 --> 00:23:50,160
Has Qi Shi contacted you?

357
00:23:53,640 --> 00:23:55,160
She's a good girl,

358
00:23:56,830 --> 00:23:58,630
keeping me updated all the time.

359
00:24:00,030 --> 00:24:02,160
She texted me just a couple of days ago,

360
00:24:02,480 --> 00:24:02,920
saying

361
00:24:03,350 --> 00:24:04,480
that she already got a job

362
00:24:04,480 --> 00:24:05,480
and settled down.

363
00:24:06,110 --> 00:24:07,770
She works in a big company now.

364
00:24:07,830 --> 00:24:09,490
What big company? Did you ask?

365
00:24:09,860 --> 00:24:10,830
No, I didn't.

366
00:24:11,400 --> 00:24:13,510
You should have.

367
00:24:14,680 --> 00:24:16,000
She's a young girl

368
00:24:16,720 --> 00:24:18,380
with no degree or experience.

369
00:24:19,000 --> 00:24:20,800
What big company would hire her?

370
00:24:21,880 --> 00:24:23,880
I hope she didn't run into scammers.

371
00:24:25,300 --> 00:24:27,200
You can't just believe
everything she says.

372
00:24:27,200 --> 00:24:27,920
You know?

373
00:24:30,590 --> 00:24:32,160
What's that smile for?

374
00:24:32,470 --> 00:24:33,790
I'm talking to you.

375
00:24:34,160 --> 00:24:35,550
Give her a call right now.

376
00:24:35,550 --> 00:24:36,550
Ask her where she is,

377
00:24:36,550 --> 00:24:37,480
where she lives,

378
00:24:37,480 --> 00:24:38,610
and where she works.

379
00:24:38,750 --> 00:24:40,480
Or else, go visit her yourself.

380
00:24:43,400 --> 00:24:44,660
Why don't you call her?

381
00:24:45,270 --> 00:24:46,070
Why should I?

382
00:24:46,070 --> 00:24:47,130
I'm busy right now.

383
00:24:47,840 --> 00:24:48,830
You've been staying

384
00:24:48,830 --> 00:24:50,290
in bed all the time lately.

385
00:24:50,310 --> 00:24:52,240
And now you're saying you're busy?

386
00:24:54,520 --> 00:24:55,680
Who's going to pay off

387
00:24:55,680 --> 00:24:56,700
our debts if I don't

388
00:24:56,700 --> 00:24:57,330
work hard?

389
00:24:57,640 --> 00:24:59,030
Neither of our kids is settled yet.

390
00:24:59,030 --> 00:24:59,960
Make room for me.

391
00:25:00,550 --> 00:25:01,550
The family will truly fall apart

392
00:25:01,550 --> 00:25:03,410
if I don't begin making money now.

393
00:25:07,440 --> 00:25:08,130
Honey,

394
00:25:08,160 --> 00:25:10,020
now that's the correct attitude.

395
00:25:10,640 --> 00:25:11,040
Right?

396
00:25:11,270 --> 00:25:13,030
This is the Huo Qinglian I know of.

397
00:25:13,030 --> 00:25:13,550
Let's

398
00:25:13,830 --> 00:25:15,460
make our family business

399
00:25:15,590 --> 00:25:16,790
bigger and stronger,

400
00:25:16,880 --> 00:25:18,720
while we wait for our kids to come home.

401
00:25:18,720 --> 00:25:19,240
Call

402
00:25:19,270 --> 00:25:20,440
Qi Shi later.

403
00:25:20,700 --> 00:25:21,640
And send some money

404
00:25:21,640 --> 00:25:22,480
to Qi Zhi.

405
00:25:22,830 --> 00:25:24,760
I'd hate for him to suffer in there.

406
00:25:25,350 --> 00:25:26,010
Yes, madam.

407
00:25:38,550 --> 00:25:40,180
[Times Square]

408
00:25:48,830 --> 00:25:49,240
Mr. He,

409
00:25:50,480 --> 00:25:52,200
this is my application
for regular employment.

410
00:25:52,200 --> 00:25:53,790
I've attached the planning data

411
00:25:53,790 --> 00:25:55,130
for the marketing department's
three hit products

412
00:25:55,130 --> 00:25:56,190
from last quarter.

413
00:25:57,550 --> 00:25:57,920
Also,

414
00:25:58,410 --> 00:25:59,690
can I get my salary

415
00:25:59,720 --> 00:26:01,450
for the internship period now?

416
00:26:05,920 --> 00:26:07,000
What do you mean by this?

417
00:26:07,000 --> 00:26:07,880
Don't you know

418
00:26:08,110 --> 00:26:08,960
what I mean?

419
00:26:09,920 --> 00:26:11,070
Here's the thing, Qi Shi.

420
00:26:11,070 --> 00:26:12,760
I let you work in our company

421
00:26:12,790 --> 00:26:14,030
simply out of pity.

422
00:26:15,000 --> 00:26:16,680
But you only finished high school,

423
00:26:16,680 --> 00:26:17,830
and you can't even make

424
00:26:17,830 --> 00:26:18,640
a basic slide.

425
00:26:19,830 --> 00:26:20,680
Do you think

426
00:26:21,160 --> 00:26:22,620
you can stay in the company

427
00:26:22,880 --> 00:26:23,830
just by some

428
00:26:24,350 --> 00:26:25,990
effortless sweet-talking?

429
00:26:26,310 --> 00:26:26,920
My money

430
00:26:26,920 --> 00:26:28,180
doesn't grow on trees.

431
00:26:28,590 --> 00:26:28,990
Right?

432
00:26:31,590 --> 00:26:33,350
You did give me a chance.

433
00:26:33,830 --> 00:26:34,630
The fact is...

434
00:26:34,680 --> 00:26:36,160
I passed the job interview

435
00:26:36,160 --> 00:26:37,250
-before...
-Hold on.

436
00:26:37,250 --> 00:26:38,200
I prepared the people

437
00:26:38,200 --> 00:26:39,400
who interviewed you.

438
00:26:40,030 --> 00:26:41,480
Otherwise, you think they'd hire you,

439
00:26:41,480 --> 00:26:42,120
who can't even tell

440
00:26:42,120 --> 00:26:43,350
the difference
between sales per square meter

441
00:26:43,350 --> 00:26:45,050
and average transaction value,

442
00:26:45,050 --> 00:26:45,970
or franchising

443
00:26:46,000 --> 00:26:47,260
and distributorship?

444
00:26:48,510 --> 00:26:49,840
Everything else aside,

445
00:26:50,070 --> 00:26:50,750
in these past few months,

446
00:26:50,750 --> 00:26:51,740
how many silly mistakes

447
00:26:51,740 --> 00:26:53,470
were caused by your ignorance?

448
00:26:53,550 --> 00:26:54,550
Do I need to remind you

449
00:26:54,550 --> 00:26:55,550
of them one by one?

450
00:27:04,440 --> 00:27:05,030
Mr. He,

451
00:27:07,000 --> 00:27:08,030
look, I...

452
00:27:08,030 --> 00:27:08,760
In addition,

453
00:27:09,510 --> 00:27:11,440
you have a severe case of albinism.

454
00:27:12,050 --> 00:27:13,350
You think people won't notice that

455
00:27:13,350 --> 00:27:14,080
when you have

456
00:27:14,400 --> 00:27:15,460
makeup and a wig on?

457
00:27:16,110 --> 00:27:17,310
How can you represent

458
00:27:18,240 --> 00:27:20,270
the company's image looking like this?

459
00:27:20,270 --> 00:27:20,960
How do you meet clients

460
00:27:20,960 --> 00:27:22,070
and negotiate with them?

461
00:27:22,070 --> 00:27:23,830
Who will take responsibility
if the clients who don't know better

462
00:27:23,830 --> 00:27:24,760
are scared away?

463
00:27:25,590 --> 00:27:26,000
Alright.

464
00:27:26,000 --> 00:27:26,600
I have tons

465
00:27:27,110 --> 00:27:27,970
of things to do.

466
00:27:28,110 --> 00:27:28,840
I'm swamped.

467
00:27:29,030 --> 00:27:30,350
Don't come back to work tomorrow.

468
00:27:30,350 --> 00:27:31,060
That's it.

469
00:27:36,750 --> 00:27:40,320
[The 5th Beining University
Debate Competition]

470
00:27:36,910 --> 00:27:38,890
Now, let's enter

471
00:27:38,920 --> 00:27:40,320
the free debate session.

472
00:27:43,590 --> 00:27:44,310
We've made

473
00:27:44,310 --> 00:27:45,440
our argument clear.

474
00:27:45,880 --> 00:27:46,550
Adversity

475
00:27:47,310 --> 00:27:48,770
builds character better,

476
00:27:49,280 --> 00:27:50,830
as it gives people the courage
to overcome

477
00:27:50,830 --> 00:27:52,200
difficulties and setbacks.

478
00:27:52,200 --> 00:27:53,270
Let's take those around us

479
00:27:53,270 --> 00:27:54,000
as examples.

480
00:27:54,480 --> 00:27:56,160
The students of humble origins who bravely

481
00:27:56,160 --> 00:27:58,070
overcame adversity
and entered our university

482
00:27:58,070 --> 00:27:59,130
are the best proof.

483
00:28:07,400 --> 00:28:08,730
Dear opposing debater,

484
00:28:09,000 --> 00:28:09,480
there is a fact

485
00:28:09,480 --> 00:28:11,280
that cannot be ignored. That is,

486
00:28:11,310 --> 00:28:13,310
poor students admitted to our school

487
00:28:13,310 --> 00:28:14,400
account for only 15%

488
00:28:14,400 --> 00:28:15,160
of the total.

489
00:28:15,720 --> 00:28:16,480
I do not deny

490
00:28:16,590 --> 00:28:18,250
that for a few, adversity does

491
00:28:18,270 --> 00:28:19,960
help build up character better.

492
00:28:19,960 --> 00:28:20,960
But compared to the positive mindset

493
00:28:20,960 --> 00:28:23,070
brought by favorable circumstances,

494
00:28:23,070 --> 00:28:23,790
adversity

495
00:28:24,270 --> 00:28:25,920
often wears down one's will

496
00:28:26,590 --> 00:28:28,190
and leaves them devastated.

497
00:28:28,350 --> 00:28:29,270
Look at these figures,

498
00:28:29,270 --> 00:28:30,510
15% versus 85%.

499
00:28:31,410 --> 00:28:32,510
The data you provided

500
00:28:32,510 --> 00:28:33,370
exactly proves

501
00:28:34,400 --> 00:28:36,480
that poverty makes it hard
to reach the top,

502
00:28:36,480 --> 00:28:39,480
while success comes easier
in favorable conditions.

503
00:28:40,440 --> 00:28:41,060
Mr. He,

504
00:28:41,200 --> 00:28:42,680
I know I've made mistakes,

505
00:28:43,040 --> 00:28:44,680
but I've been working diligently
for the past six months

506
00:28:44,680 --> 00:28:46,240
without slacking off.

507
00:28:46,400 --> 00:28:47,850
You said you had to delay the payroll

508
00:28:47,850 --> 00:28:49,180
due to cash flow issues.

509
00:28:49,680 --> 00:28:51,070
But I should at least get my pay

510
00:28:51,070 --> 00:28:52,310
for working here

511
00:28:52,350 --> 00:28:52,830
for six months.

512
00:28:52,830 --> 00:28:54,000
Do you have to nag on and on?

513
00:28:54,000 --> 00:28:55,120
You're just a high school graduate.

514
00:28:55,120 --> 00:28:56,000
You don't meet the company's

515
00:28:56,000 --> 00:28:57,310
hiring requirements at all.

516
00:28:57,310 --> 00:28:57,770
Also, by

517
00:28:58,200 --> 00:28:59,790
withholding the fact
that you have a major illness

518
00:28:59,790 --> 00:29:01,580
from the company, I can sue you anytime.

519
00:29:01,580 --> 00:29:03,240
How dare you ask me for you pay?

520
00:29:03,720 --> 00:29:04,780
Pack up your things

521
00:29:04,790 --> 00:29:06,310
and leave the staff dorm immediately.

522
00:29:06,310 --> 00:29:06,970
Otherwise,

523
00:29:07,680 --> 00:29:09,140
I won't show you any mercy.

524
00:29:09,640 --> 00:29:10,100
Get out!

525
00:29:12,750 --> 00:29:13,720
I agree with

526
00:29:13,750 --> 00:29:15,010
the opposing debater.

527
00:29:15,680 --> 00:29:16,720
Figures are cold.

528
00:29:18,200 --> 00:29:19,070
I'd like to take a girl

529
00:29:19,070 --> 00:29:20,200
I know as an example.

530
00:29:21,240 --> 00:29:22,640
I grew up with a neighbor.

531
00:29:24,440 --> 00:29:25,840
In terms of grades alone,

532
00:29:26,440 --> 00:29:28,440
she was almost always in first place.

533
00:29:28,440 --> 00:29:31,240
She definitely met
all the standards for success.

534
00:29:31,370 --> 00:29:32,610
But she didn't finish

535
00:29:32,640 --> 00:29:34,100
the college entrance exam

536
00:29:34,400 --> 00:29:35,860
due to a family emergency.

537
00:29:35,960 --> 00:29:37,890
She couldn't even repeat the year.

538
00:29:40,030 --> 00:29:42,630
So she had no choice
but to enter society early.

539
00:29:42,920 --> 00:29:43,550
Compared to us,

540
00:29:43,550 --> 00:29:45,160
who are talking eloquently

541
00:29:45,720 --> 00:29:47,380
on a college debate stage now,

542
00:29:47,590 --> 00:29:48,400
she is probably

543
00:29:48,400 --> 00:29:50,000
struggling to make a living.

544
00:29:53,240 --> 00:29:54,900
Given that, think about this.

545
00:29:57,000 --> 00:29:59,000
Who should be considered a success,

546
00:30:01,070 --> 00:30:02,870
me in favorable circumstances,

547
00:30:04,640 --> 00:30:05,960
or her in adversity?

548
00:30:08,790 --> 00:30:09,390
Thank you.

549
00:30:21,590 --> 00:30:22,240
Qi Shi.

550
00:30:23,790 --> 00:30:24,440
Qi Shi!

551
00:30:25,310 --> 00:30:26,070
Wait, Qi Shi!

552
00:30:29,070 --> 00:30:30,600
You left something behind.

553
00:30:32,270 --> 00:30:32,870
Thank you.

554
00:30:38,450 --> 00:30:39,140
Come here.

555
00:30:44,440 --> 00:30:45,840
Let me tell you the truth.

556
00:30:46,440 --> 00:30:48,970
Since the first day
you started working here,

557
00:30:49,090 --> 00:30:50,030
Mr. He has never thought

558
00:30:50,030 --> 00:30:51,090
about keeping you.

559
00:30:51,480 --> 00:30:53,540
It's typical of him to use this trick.

560
00:30:53,550 --> 00:30:55,800
He just exploited you as an intern

561
00:30:55,830 --> 00:30:57,070
for free labor.

562
00:30:57,440 --> 00:30:58,270
Not just you,

563
00:30:58,750 --> 00:31:00,850
but several college students
were dismissed

564
00:31:00,850 --> 00:31:02,130
with various excuses

565
00:31:02,160 --> 00:31:02,890
previously.

566
00:31:03,240 --> 00:31:04,390
It's illegal to fire us

567
00:31:04,390 --> 00:31:05,810
without proper cause.

568
00:31:05,960 --> 00:31:07,030
Even if Mr. He hires new staffers,

569
00:31:07,030 --> 00:31:08,990
he still has to pay compensation
for wrongful termination.

570
00:31:08,990 --> 00:31:10,320
Don't get all worked up.

571
00:31:11,510 --> 00:31:12,770
Given your condition,

572
00:31:12,880 --> 00:31:14,410
it's a bit hard to find a job.

573
00:31:14,440 --> 00:31:16,300
But there will always be a way out.

574
00:31:17,070 --> 00:31:19,400
I didn't mean to
keep my albinism a secret.

575
00:31:20,090 --> 00:31:21,620
I can just work as well
with this condition.

576
00:31:21,620 --> 00:31:22,350
It's just...

577
00:31:23,240 --> 00:31:24,770
that I didn't go to college,

578
00:31:26,030 --> 00:31:28,160
and that it's so hard
for me to get a job.

579
00:31:28,750 --> 00:31:29,440
Listen.

580
00:31:30,640 --> 00:31:32,880
Though we were colleagues
for just six months,

581
00:31:32,880 --> 00:31:34,540
I do think of you as a smart girl

582
00:31:34,790 --> 00:31:35,850
and a fast learner.

583
00:31:36,420 --> 00:31:37,160
You are no less

584
00:31:37,160 --> 00:31:38,820
than those college students.

585
00:31:39,110 --> 00:31:39,880
Besides,

586
00:31:40,450 --> 00:31:41,310
from my professional

587
00:31:41,310 --> 00:31:42,840
perspective as a designer,

588
00:31:43,160 --> 00:31:45,200
I'd say you have a great aesthetic.

589
00:31:45,840 --> 00:31:47,480
If you want to stay in the industry

590
00:31:47,480 --> 00:31:49,250
of women's fashion...

591
00:31:49,920 --> 00:31:52,120
I got to know an older lady some time ago.

592
00:31:52,170 --> 00:31:52,830
She's planning

593
00:31:52,830 --> 00:31:54,230
to close her shop lately.

594
00:31:54,680 --> 00:31:57,350
So, she needs to dump some stock,
even at a discount.

595
00:31:57,350 --> 00:31:58,170
How about...

596
00:31:58,440 --> 00:32:00,720
you take it over

597
00:32:01,350 --> 00:32:02,270
and resell it?

598
00:32:02,550 --> 00:32:03,810
That could be a way out.

599
00:32:05,830 --> 00:32:06,430
I'll do it.

600
00:32:07,160 --> 00:32:07,890
I'm up for it.

601
00:32:08,000 --> 00:32:09,330
This is great. Thank...

602
00:32:11,200 --> 00:32:12,110
I-I'm sorry.

603
00:32:21,550 --> 00:32:22,350
My illness...

604
00:32:23,550 --> 00:32:24,680
doesn't bother you?

605
00:32:24,880 --> 00:32:26,400
I do have basic common sense.

606
00:32:26,400 --> 00:32:26,930
Alright?

607
00:32:30,590 --> 00:32:31,000
Okay.

608
00:32:31,440 --> 00:32:32,040
Yuanyuan,

609
00:32:32,160 --> 00:32:33,110
you're the first friend

610
00:32:33,110 --> 00:32:34,380
I made in Haizhou.

611
00:32:35,510 --> 00:32:36,970
May our paths cross again.

612
00:32:37,480 --> 00:32:38,550
That will happen.

613
00:32:40,510 --> 00:32:41,110
Off you go.

614
00:32:43,590 --> 00:32:44,130
Goodbye.

615
00:33:01,710 --> 00:33:03,160
[Dear ringtone user,
since today is your birthday,

616
00:33:03,160 --> 00:33:04,610
we're offering you one month
of free ringtone replacement]

617
00:33:08,990 --> 00:33:10,510
[Change it to Can't Help Loving You]

618
00:33:20,070 --> 00:33:20,630
Honey,

619
00:33:21,160 --> 00:33:23,000
look, our shop has stepped

620
00:33:24,000 --> 00:33:25,590
on the right track now.

621
00:33:26,030 --> 00:33:27,230
I'm just thinking...

622
00:33:28,330 --> 00:33:30,150
maybe we should move to Haizhou.

623
00:33:31,440 --> 00:33:32,430
We can replicate

624
00:33:32,960 --> 00:33:34,680
our successful business mode

625
00:33:34,900 --> 00:33:36,370
at that place.

626
00:33:37,240 --> 00:33:37,790
You see,

627
00:33:38,920 --> 00:33:40,180
it's much bigger there

628
00:33:40,880 --> 00:33:42,340
with a higher population.

629
00:33:42,370 --> 00:33:42,920
So it must be

630
00:33:42,920 --> 00:33:45,050
easier to do business there than here.

631
00:33:45,920 --> 00:33:46,680
Besides,

632
00:33:47,160 --> 00:33:48,110
haven't you always

633
00:33:48,110 --> 00:33:49,310
wanted to move there?

634
00:33:49,350 --> 00:33:50,680
You think I have no idea?

635
00:33:50,870 --> 00:33:51,860
You want to move there

636
00:33:51,860 --> 00:33:54,190
s-so you can check on our daughter, right?

637
00:33:55,440 --> 00:33:57,040
Am I the only one missing her?

638
00:33:59,480 --> 00:34:00,740
Don't you miss her too?

639
00:34:04,310 --> 00:34:05,510
Otherwise, why would you fry so many

640
00:34:05,510 --> 00:34:06,170
mushrooms?

641
00:34:07,110 --> 00:34:08,469
I fried them for you!

642
00:34:08,800 --> 00:34:09,780
I fried them just for you.

643
00:34:09,780 --> 00:34:10,630
Make sure you finish

644
00:34:10,630 --> 00:34:11,800
all of them yourself.

645
00:34:11,800 --> 00:34:12,130
Okay.

646
00:34:12,590 --> 00:34:13,389
I'll eat them.

647
00:34:14,030 --> 00:34:15,290
W-What about the buns?

648
00:34:16,550 --> 00:34:17,949
Are they also just for me?

649
00:34:19,550 --> 00:34:21,080
Then I'd say I'm very lucky.

650
00:34:22,400 --> 00:34:24,400
Stop saying that.

651
00:34:24,550 --> 00:34:26,030
How are you lucky?

652
00:34:26,530 --> 00:34:27,989
It's been over six months,

653
00:34:28,480 --> 00:34:30,920
yet our daughter has never answered
your calls,

654
00:34:30,920 --> 00:34:32,850
and our son wouldn't  meet with you.

655
00:34:33,280 --> 00:34:35,139
After living for such a long time,

656
00:34:35,770 --> 00:34:36,980
you are stuck with me

657
00:34:37,030 --> 00:34:38,230
at the end of the day.

658
00:34:39,070 --> 00:34:40,840
What's the point of our lives?

659
00:34:43,710 --> 00:34:44,510
To be honest,

660
00:34:45,440 --> 00:34:46,590
I have a hunch

661
00:34:47,960 --> 00:34:49,280
that Qi Shi will give me

662
00:34:49,550 --> 00:34:50,710
a call today.

663
00:34:51,110 --> 00:34:52,360
Come on, stop with it.

664
00:34:52,900 --> 00:34:54,130
The buns are ready.

665
00:34:54,400 --> 00:34:55,659
Pack them up quickly.

666
00:34:55,770 --> 00:34:57,400
Lingzhi's cousin is delivering

667
00:34:57,400 --> 00:34:58,730
goods to Haizhou later.

668
00:34:58,880 --> 00:35:00,540
Ask him to take the food there.

669
00:35:00,920 --> 00:35:02,720
What about the fried mushrooms?

670
00:35:07,440 --> 00:35:10,100
It's a pity
that we're too far away from Beining.

671
00:35:12,510 --> 00:35:13,170
Otherwise,

672
00:35:13,230 --> 00:35:15,550
I'll definitely have these
brought to Cao Xin.

673
00:35:15,550 --> 00:35:16,400
Today is his birthday.

674
00:35:16,400 --> 00:35:17,800
He must be craving these.

675
00:35:21,880 --> 00:35:23,610
Our children have all grown up.

676
00:35:24,070 --> 00:35:26,000
We can't reach or see them anymore.

677
00:35:26,810 --> 00:35:27,880
Even if we want to show them we care,

678
00:35:27,880 --> 00:35:29,480
we don't know where to start.

679
00:35:43,760 --> 00:35:44,150
Dad.

680
00:35:44,480 --> 00:35:45,030
Son,

681
00:35:45,360 --> 00:35:47,000
did you get the birthday gift

682
00:35:47,030 --> 00:35:47,710
I sent you?

683
00:35:48,000 --> 00:35:48,590
Yes, I did.

684
00:35:48,590 --> 00:35:49,650
I got it yesterday.

685
00:35:50,190 --> 00:35:51,450
Have you opened it yet?

686
00:35:53,410 --> 00:35:54,550
I had classes all day today.

687
00:35:54,550 --> 00:35:56,280
I haven't had time to open it yet.

688
00:35:56,280 --> 00:35:56,940
No worries.

689
00:35:56,950 --> 00:35:57,510
I just placed

690
00:35:57,510 --> 00:35:59,040
some study materials in it.

691
00:36:00,110 --> 00:36:01,310
I've checked online.

692
00:36:01,880 --> 00:36:03,080
The finance program

693
00:36:03,110 --> 00:36:03,880
at MacDonald University

694
00:36:03,880 --> 00:36:05,320
is really, really good.

695
00:36:05,760 --> 00:36:06,690
You need to start

696
00:36:06,800 --> 00:36:07,930
planning right now.

697
00:36:08,280 --> 00:36:09,510
Make sure you master both

698
00:36:09,510 --> 00:36:11,110
the language and your major.

699
00:36:11,760 --> 00:36:12,590
You will go abroad

700
00:36:12,590 --> 00:36:15,120
for further studies
the moment you graduate.

701
00:36:15,360 --> 00:36:16,020
Got it, Dad.

702
00:36:17,400 --> 00:36:17,920
Cao Xin!

703
00:36:18,150 --> 00:36:18,800
Cao Xin!

704
00:36:18,800 --> 00:36:20,510
-You are really something.
-Look.

705
00:36:20,510 --> 00:36:21,670
Impressive, man.

706
00:36:22,320 --> 00:36:23,580
Your birthday is known

707
00:36:23,710 --> 00:36:26,110
to all the girls
in the School of Economics.

708
00:36:27,900 --> 00:36:28,530
Wait, how did you

709
00:36:28,530 --> 00:36:29,590
get all this stuff?

710
00:36:30,000 --> 00:36:30,880
Didn't I tell the dorm supervisor

711
00:36:30,880 --> 00:36:31,810
to reject these?

712
00:36:32,690 --> 00:36:33,920
The dorm supervisor did as you said.

713
00:36:33,920 --> 00:36:35,480
But we dared not refuse the girls.

714
00:36:35,480 --> 00:36:36,340
Think about it.

715
00:36:36,590 --> 00:36:37,810
The debate competition

716
00:36:37,810 --> 00:36:38,710
has shown that the girls

717
00:36:38,710 --> 00:36:40,320
in the School of Economics
are sharp-tongued.

718
00:36:40,320 --> 00:36:41,280
For the sake of unity

719
00:36:41,280 --> 00:36:43,150
and the friendship among fellow students,

720
00:36:43,150 --> 00:36:44,010
we had no choice

721
00:36:44,230 --> 00:36:45,110
but to accept

722
00:36:45,370 --> 00:36:46,230
the girls' gifts

723
00:36:46,230 --> 00:36:47,090
on your behalf.

724
00:36:47,210 --> 00:36:47,710
Your...

725
00:36:48,150 --> 00:36:50,070
Is this how you treat a good friend?

726
00:36:50,070 --> 00:36:51,480
Look how many items you took.

727
00:36:51,480 --> 00:36:52,140
Hey, bro...

728
00:36:54,280 --> 00:36:55,880
Look at this trophy of yours.

729
00:36:56,090 --> 00:36:57,600
You're good at everything

730
00:36:57,630 --> 00:36:58,640
and you always rank first.

731
00:36:58,640 --> 00:36:59,850
You're the pride

732
00:36:59,880 --> 00:37:00,760
of Room 206.

733
00:37:01,030 --> 00:37:01,760
Exactly!

734
00:37:01,960 --> 00:37:02,560
Fine then.

735
00:37:02,960 --> 00:37:04,230
I'll treat you guys to dinner,

736
00:37:04,230 --> 00:37:04,590
okay?

737
00:37:04,880 --> 00:37:05,710
Just stop teasing me,

738
00:37:05,710 --> 00:37:06,250
will you?

739
00:37:06,280 --> 00:37:07,410
-Sure.
-No problem.

740
00:37:07,440 --> 00:37:08,840
That was what we waited to hear.

741
00:37:08,840 --> 00:37:09,590
I'm on the phone with my dad.

742
00:37:09,590 --> 00:37:10,650
Keep it down, guys.

743
00:37:12,320 --> 00:37:12,710
Dad.

744
00:37:13,400 --> 00:37:14,060
Son, you are

745
00:37:14,200 --> 00:37:15,230
having dinner with your classmates

746
00:37:15,230 --> 00:37:16,160
tonight, right?

747
00:37:16,590 --> 00:37:17,840
Do you have enough money?

748
00:37:17,840 --> 00:37:18,370
Yes, yes.

749
00:37:18,920 --> 00:37:20,510
I just received a scholarship.

750
00:37:20,510 --> 00:37:20,920
Great.

751
00:37:21,150 --> 00:37:23,350
Have a good time celebrating with them.

752
00:37:23,760 --> 00:37:24,480
Is it Xin?

753
00:37:25,280 --> 00:37:25,630
Yes.

754
00:37:26,280 --> 00:37:27,010
Well...

755
00:37:28,110 --> 00:37:28,550
Son,

756
00:37:29,000 --> 00:37:30,550
you really should spend more time

757
00:37:30,550 --> 00:37:32,710
with your classmates when you're free.

758
00:37:32,710 --> 00:37:33,510
See if there is a girl

759
00:37:33,510 --> 00:37:34,640
who is right for you.

760
00:37:35,110 --> 00:37:36,780
You're a college student now.

761
00:37:37,670 --> 00:37:39,190
I won't object to you dating someone

762
00:37:39,190 --> 00:37:40,630
as long as it doesn't affect

763
00:37:40,630 --> 00:37:41,400
your studies.

764
00:37:41,400 --> 00:37:42,660
That's right, Xin!

765
00:37:43,590 --> 00:37:44,590
Listen to me.

766
00:37:45,140 --> 00:37:46,500
You must study hard.

767
00:37:46,670 --> 00:37:47,560
You can find

768
00:37:47,590 --> 00:37:48,920
all the answers in books!

769
00:37:48,920 --> 00:37:49,910
Got it, Grandpa.

770
00:37:50,590 --> 00:37:51,850
Take care of yourself.

771
00:37:53,440 --> 00:37:53,970
Alright.

772
00:37:54,110 --> 00:37:54,970
I'm hanging up.

773
00:37:55,550 --> 00:37:55,960
Bye.

774
00:37:56,760 --> 00:37:57,360
He hung up.

775
00:37:58,970 --> 00:37:59,900
Of course he did.

776
00:38:00,110 --> 00:38:00,480
Dad,

777
00:38:01,070 --> 00:38:02,760
stop talking about superstitions

778
00:38:02,760 --> 00:38:03,820
with young people.

779
00:38:04,010 --> 00:38:04,590
They just don't

780
00:38:04,590 --> 00:38:05,720
believe that stuff.

781
00:38:10,440 --> 00:38:11,040
Dongfang,

782
00:38:12,690 --> 00:38:14,890
I keep thinking about one thing lately.

783
00:38:16,440 --> 00:38:17,770
In the past, every year,

784
00:38:18,800 --> 00:38:20,330
Xin's birthday always came

785
00:38:22,030 --> 00:38:23,630
right after Si's.

786
00:38:29,960 --> 00:38:31,420
Time to feed the chickens.

787
00:38:47,320 --> 00:38:48,250
Happy birthday.

788
00:38:55,240 --> 00:38:56,550
Why do I have to celebrate my birthday

789
00:38:56,550 --> 00:38:58,100
with Cao Xin every year?

790
00:38:58,400 --> 00:38:59,860
Why can't we just buy a cake

791
00:39:00,190 --> 00:39:00,760
and celebrate

792
00:39:00,760 --> 00:39:02,290
at home like we do it for Zhi?

793
00:39:02,710 --> 00:39:03,640
You're so fussy.

794
00:39:03,720 --> 00:39:04,800
You two share the same birthday.

795
00:39:04,800 --> 00:39:06,400
It's more fun to celebrate together.

796
00:39:06,400 --> 00:39:06,960
Sweetie,

797
00:39:07,110 --> 00:39:08,040
come take a look.

798
00:39:08,440 --> 00:39:09,170
What's this?

799
00:39:09,280 --> 00:39:10,010
You're here.

800
00:39:10,280 --> 00:39:11,410
Come on, take a look.

801
00:39:12,000 --> 00:39:12,800
Here it goes.

802
00:39:13,110 --> 00:39:17,000
♪ Happy birthday to you ♪

803
00:39:17,630 --> 00:39:21,480
♪ Happy birthday to you ♪

804
00:39:23,150 --> 00:39:23,590
Feifei!

805
00:39:23,590 --> 00:39:24,400
Thank you.

806
00:39:24,800 --> 00:39:25,460
Qingcheng.

807
00:39:27,630 --> 00:39:28,800
I invited Qingcheng over.

808
00:39:28,800 --> 00:39:30,730
Hope you don't mind an extra guest.

809
00:39:31,670 --> 00:39:32,840
Isn't she Gu Qingcheng, the golden girl

810
00:39:32,840 --> 00:39:34,110
of the School of Economics?

811
00:39:34,110 --> 00:39:34,960
Your presence

812
00:39:35,010 --> 00:39:35,630
has lightened up

813
00:39:35,630 --> 00:39:36,960
this little cafeteria.

814
00:39:37,110 --> 00:39:38,480
That's an exaggeration.

815
00:39:38,480 --> 00:39:39,190
How could I steal

816
00:39:39,190 --> 00:39:40,320
the spotlight from the birthday boy?

817
00:39:40,320 --> 00:39:40,840
Not at all.

818
00:39:40,840 --> 00:39:41,510
Have a seat.

819
00:39:41,880 --> 00:39:42,920
Grab her a chair now.

820
00:39:42,920 --> 00:39:43,920
Just take my seat.

821
00:39:49,600 --> 00:39:51,200
Time to blow out the candles.

822
00:39:59,480 --> 00:40:00,300
You two birthday stars,

823
00:40:00,300 --> 00:40:01,230
make a wish.

824
00:40:03,590 --> 00:40:04,790
What did you wish for?

825
00:40:10,770 --> 00:40:12,370
Happy birthday!

826
00:40:12,400 --> 00:40:14,530
-Happy birthday.
-Let's cut the cake!

827
00:40:14,550 --> 00:40:15,070
Alright.

828
00:40:15,070 --> 00:40:15,530
Come on.

829
00:40:18,710 --> 00:40:19,440
There we go.

830
00:40:19,680 --> 00:40:20,710
You're about to lose your front tooth.

831
00:40:20,710 --> 00:40:21,710
Keep the flowers.

832
00:40:22,030 --> 00:40:22,960
One for each kid.

833
00:40:22,960 --> 00:40:23,670
Give it to Qi Shi first.

834
00:40:23,670 --> 00:40:24,510
Okay, Qi Shi first.

835
00:40:24,510 --> 00:40:24,840
Okay.

836
00:40:25,360 --> 00:40:25,880
Here you are.

837
00:40:25,880 --> 00:40:27,110
-This piece is for Cao Xin.
-Cao Xin!

838
00:40:27,110 --> 00:40:27,670
Okay.

839
00:40:28,880 --> 00:40:29,840
And this piece...

840
00:40:29,840 --> 00:40:30,920
-is for Qi Zhi.
-Give it to Grandpa.

841
00:40:30,920 --> 00:40:31,590
Okay. For Grandpa.

842
00:40:31,590 --> 00:40:32,630
Give it to Grandpa.

843
00:40:32,630 --> 00:40:33,630
-Alright, thanks.
-This is for the elderly.

844
00:40:33,630 --> 00:40:34,360
T-Take it.

845
00:40:36,320 --> 00:40:37,360
Cao Xin!

846
00:40:37,410 --> 00:40:38,280
Take this out.

847
00:40:39,000 --> 00:40:39,800
Come back here!

848
00:40:39,800 --> 00:40:40,930
What just happened?

849
00:40:43,510 --> 00:40:44,770
What wish did you make?

850
00:40:45,990 --> 00:40:48,330
Nothing in particular.

851
00:40:48,360 --> 00:40:50,200
I just thought of

852
00:40:50,230 --> 00:40:51,190
a childhood friend.

853
00:40:51,190 --> 00:40:52,110
I'd really like to spend

854
00:40:52,110 --> 00:40:53,570
a birthday with her again.

855
00:40:54,440 --> 00:40:55,590
A childhood friend?

856
00:40:56,570 --> 00:40:57,720
You mean...

857
00:40:57,780 --> 00:40:58,730
the neighbor

858
00:40:58,760 --> 00:41:00,360
you mentioned at the debate?

859
00:41:01,480 --> 00:41:01,980
Yes.

860
00:41:04,280 --> 00:41:05,410
What does she do now?

861
00:41:06,800 --> 00:41:08,800
We've been out of touch for a long time.

862
00:41:08,800 --> 00:41:09,660
So I don't know.

863
00:41:11,170 --> 00:41:12,730
If it's meant to be,

864
00:41:12,760 --> 00:41:13,960
you'll see her again.

865
00:41:15,190 --> 00:41:15,720
Perhaps.

866
00:41:19,760 --> 00:41:20,690
Noodles for you.

867
00:41:20,840 --> 00:41:21,630
Thank you,

868
00:41:34,200 --> 00:41:34,640
ma'am.

869
00:41:34,740 --> 00:41:35,800
A bowl of beef noodles!

870
00:41:35,800 --> 00:41:36,730
Coming right up.

871
00:41:37,300 --> 00:41:38,450
[Dad]

872
00:41:54,550 --> 00:41:55,150
Sweetie,

873
00:41:55,670 --> 00:41:57,000
today is your birthday.

874
00:41:57,070 --> 00:41:58,590
Your mom made you fried mushrooms

875
00:41:58,590 --> 00:41:59,590
and steamed buns.

876
00:41:59,770 --> 00:42:00,710
We had them brought

877
00:42:00,710 --> 00:42:01,770
to Haizhou for you.

878
00:42:02,150 --> 00:42:03,500
You're still at the address you sent me

879
00:42:03,500 --> 00:42:04,430
earlier, right?

880
00:42:07,550 --> 00:42:08,030
Dad,

881
00:42:08,510 --> 00:42:10,170
I'm no longer at that address.

882
00:42:10,880 --> 00:42:12,360
As for the new address...

883
00:42:45,110 --> 00:42:45,670
Hello?

884
00:42:46,840 --> 00:42:47,800
Hello, Dad.

885
00:42:48,960 --> 00:42:49,510
Sweetie,

886
00:42:50,110 --> 00:42:51,840
you finally called.

887
00:42:52,840 --> 00:42:53,670
I knew

888
00:42:53,950 --> 00:42:55,520
my hunch was right.

889
00:42:57,000 --> 00:42:58,860
Have you eaten birthday cake yet?

890
00:42:59,450 --> 00:43:01,160
And those fried mushrooms

891
00:43:01,190 --> 00:43:02,320
and steamed buns...

892
00:43:02,550 --> 00:43:03,400
Have you got them?
